  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Talk the defence into place",
  "description": "Play 5 v 5 to 7 v 7 with goals and goalkeepers. Before you start, each team agrees on a few short defending words that everyone understands, for example \"I'm going!\" (I press), \"Cover!\" (I'm behind you), a name plus \"Yours!\" (you take that player) and \"Up!\" (the line steps up). The diagram shows four outfield players per team.\n\nFirst play a short round where nobody may talk at all. Then play with free talk. The defending team gets an extra point every time it wins the ball after a clear call with a name. The coach can stop play and ask the nearest player what was said. Ask after the rounds as well: what was the difference?\n\nPlay offside sometimes if you do in matches – it changes what needs to be said. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Say the name first, so the right person listens – then the word."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Short, loud and in time. Say it before it happens, not after."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Only use the words you have agreed on. Everyone should understand them the same way."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "The goalkeeper sees the most and should organise the line from behind."
    }
  ],
